# What Vercel does NOT need to deploy.
#
#   The repository carries 158 MB of property photographs, plus source, docs and test material.
#   None of it is read by the running server: the images are served to the browser by a 302 in
#   vercel.json that points at raw.githubusercontent.com, the v2 source is already built into
#   public/v2, and the tests never run in production. Vercel stores every deployment it has ever
#   made, so anything listed here is a few hundred megabytes NOT kept for each one.
#
#   Keep in mind when adding a line: server-complete.js reads public/ and data/ at runtime and
#   imports lib/, properties/ and image-urls.js, so none of those may be excluded.
#
#   EVERY DIRECTORY LINE IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and it must stay that way. These
#   patterns follow .gitignore rules, where a bare `v2/` matches a directory called v2 at ANY
#   depth - so it also matched `public/v2/`, the BUILT atlas the server serves at `/`. From
#   V0.44 (17 Sep 2026) until V0.52 every deployment therefore shipped without the atlas, and
#   `/` quietly fell back to the classic Leaflet page: `serveV2` catches the missing file and
#   serves `/classic` instead, so nothing errored and nothing in the logs said so. The sandbox
#   cannot open *.vercel.app, which is why the tests never caught it either. `/v2/` excludes
#   the SOURCE at the repository root and leaves the build alone.

/images/
/attached_assets/
/docs/
/tests/
/v2/
/bmr/
/brochures/
*.py
*.md
!README.md
/.github/
